runner-debug.dSYM/
# build scratch. Also holds .build/template-oracles/ — the upstream jinja chat
# templates `make template-conformance` fetches to compare runner's native C
# renderer against. They are vendor files under each model's own license, so
# they are cached, never committed; the sha256 of each one IS committed, in
# scripts/template-conformance-baseline.json, so an upstream change is still
# visible. NOTE `make clean` removes this whole directory, which means the
# next conformance run re-fetches (network, plus models/ for the GGUF-sourced
# families). That is why the gate is not wired into `make test`.
.build/
